DTO = Data Transfer Object.

It’s a small, dumb data container you use to move data across
boundaries (service → controller → API response) without exposing your
domain models or leaking internal structure. Think: “the exact shape I
want to return (or accept), nothing more, nothing less.”

Why use a DTO (vs arrays or models)?

Stable API shape — you control exactly what leaves your service.

No domain leakage — callers can’t mutate your models or rely on
internal fields.

Type-safety & autocompletion — better than loose assoc arrays.

Easy versioning — add a new DTO or fields without touching models.

Testable — DTO equality/assertions are straightforward.

<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Dto;

use JsonSerializable;

final class BiblePassageDto implements JsonSerializable
{
    public function __construct(
        public readonly string $reference,   // e.g. "Luke 15:11–24"
        /** @var list<array{v:int,t:string}> */
        public readonly array $verses,       // [{v:11,t:"..."}]
        public readonly string $bibleCode,   // e.g. "ENGESV"
        public readonly ?string $copyright,  // optional
        public readonly ?string $footnotes   // optional
    ) {}

    /** @return array<string,mixed> */
    public function toArray(): array
    {
        return [
            'reference' => $this->reference,
            'verses'    => $this->verses,
            'bibleCode' => $this->bibleCode,
            'copyright' => $this->copyright,
            'footnotes' => $this->footnotes,
        ];
    }

    public function jsonSerialize(): array
    {
        return $this->toArray();
    }
}

A small mapper keeps domain separate from DTO shape:

<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Mappers;

use App\Dto\BiblePassageDto;
use App\Models\Bible\PassageModel;

final class BiblePassageMapper
{
    public static function fromModel(
        PassageModel $model,
        string $bibleCode
    ): BiblePassageDto {
        // Convert your model into the exact outbound shape.
        $verses = [];
        foreach ($model->getVerses() as $v) {
            $verses[] = ['v' => (int)$v->number, 't' => (string)$v->text];
        }

        return new BiblePassageDto(
            reference: $model->getReference(),
            verses:    $verses,
            bibleCode: $bibleCode,
            copyright: $model->getCopyright(),
            footnotes: $model->getFootnotes()
        );
    }
}

Then your service returns a DTO (not a model, not a raw array):

$passageModel = $this->biblePassageService->getPassage(
    $this->primaryBibleModel,
    $this->passageReferenceInfo
);

$passageDto = BiblePassageMapper::fromModel(
    $passageModel,
    $this->primaryBibleModel->getCode()
);

return [
    'bibleBlock' => [
        'template'       => $template,
        'primaryPassage' => $passageDto->toArray(), // or return $passageDto and let controller serialize
    ],
];

